# L3 Data-Hygiene Rules

Source: *Advances in Financial ML* [AFML] Ch.4/7/12, *Algorithmic Trading*
[Chan] Ch.1. See `docs/QUANT_ARCHITECTURE.md` Part II.

- **Strict point-in-time.** Retrieval targeting a moment MUST use a STRICT
  inequality (`date < as_of`). The predicted match and everything after it are
  invisible. No look-ahead bias is permitted, ever [AFML, Chan].
- **No model math here.** `FeatureStore` MUST NOT import any model or contain
  Poisson/Elo/Kelly/pricing logic. It returns structured, timestamped frames;
  models own all statistics.
- **Label intervals.** Features built from rolling/look-back windows MUST carry
  an information interval `(info_start, resolve_time)` for downstream purging.
- **Purge + embargo.** CV training sets MUST be PURGED of observations whose
  interval overlaps the test interval [AFML 7.1], and an EMBARGO applied after
  each test fold [AFML 7.2].
- **No standard K-Fold.** `sklearn.KFold`, `cross_val_score`, and
  `train_test_split(shuffle=True)` on temporal data are BANNED. Use
  PurgedKFold / Combinatorial Purged CV [AFML 7.3, 12].
- **Not IID.** Weight overlapping observations by average uniqueness, not equally
  [AFML 4]; combine with recency decay.

```python
# ✅ strict, leakage-free
train = store.training_frame(as_of=kickoff)   # keeps date < kickoff only
# ❌ banned for time series
from sklearn.model_selection import KFold     # NO
```
